   {
    "title": "All-in-One Network Station (Senior Design Project)",
    "description": "Collaborated with a team of 6 students to design a compact PC workstation system intended for managing Cisco routers in remote test sites.\n\nDesigned and built a KVM (keyboard, video, and mouse) switch based on the Raspberry Pi Pico microcontroller board with KiCAD schematic capture and PCB design software, capable of quickly switching USB and DisplayPort signals, controlled via physical buttons or UART serial commands.",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": ""
   },
   {
    "title": "Convolution Reverb",
    "description": "Project for CPE 431 - Introduction: Computer Architecture\n\nWrote a MATLAB script implementing a convolution reverb algorithm, taking an input audio file and impulse response and generating an output .wav file with an configurable reverberation effect.\n\nGave an engaging and well-received presentation of the project, thoroughly explaining the concepts involved and showing audio samples to demonstrate its functionality.",
